  "scope": "two-READ-target profile (Claude_Two_READ_Targets_Hardware_Directive.md): mixed READ (one request, g1v2 q00 0-15 + g30v1 q00 0-7) 91->141 as [50, 91] with 26 G1V2 points 1024..1049, and the base-database full READ (integrity poll) 247->271 as [24, 247] with 4 points 1024..1027, both by the pipe-1 prefix construction; SELECT/OPERATE 37->61 unchanged. By declaration: the range READ keeps m11_09 admission and timing and passes at native 49 (not padded); analog and class0 READ requests are NOT admitted by N (their admission was replaced by the mixed one, m12p_c23): on an admitted connection N withholds them, also when retransmitted, forwarding nothing either way and leaving the connection state unchanged (measured on the model, two_read_robust X), so a master that issues one stalls until its application times out; the native two-segment 377 response is out of scope. READ responses are admitted by N first block only (link and block-0 CRCs checked; TCP checksum WAIVED -- m.tcp_sum written 0xffeb -- not computed); resource-reduced (m12p_c26): pipe-1 block-0 CRC by residue, outcome/IP-length/checksum conditions set where decided, unreachable E read_b0 CRC compares removed -- behavior unchanged; m12p_c27 (F1): a pure ACK (kind 3 master, kind 10 outstation) that finds the N work cell busy is retried on the 32-lap budget instead of busy_pass (which E dropped); count_busy[6] counts retries; m12p_c28: a READ request that overtakes the final handshake ACK (owner phase 4, sequence check passing) is admitted as completing the handshake instead of refused; the late pure ACK is dropped; m12p_c29: pipe-0 headroom -- N and E highest occupied stage index 10 (placement pins, two identity hashes as copies, control CRC tails under the control-pad gate) -- behavior unchanged",
